  "note": "Three hand-authored personas for the OKR tracker's seven-axis composite grader. gradeObjective(a) is deliberately pure: all date maths (committed-at-risk, stale-check-in) use a.now, a field ON THE ASSESSMENT ITSELF, never the wall clock - these personas set it explicitly rather than relying on the oracle's frozen clock. Progress and confidence/alignment/smart/pace all default a null score to 'amber' (a documented-as-unknown state) WITH a rule (unlike issue-tracker, which pushes no rule for a null score); stretch and impact are purely informational and always band 'green' regardless of value. Progress thresholds depend on stretchTier: tier 1 (committed) needs >=70% for green and is red below 50%; tier 2 (aspirational) is green at >=30%, red below 10%; tier 3 (moonshot) is green at >=25% with no red floor. Twelve independent flag checks run regardless of the composite band; several require BOTH a condition and populated cycle dates (committed-at-risk, stale-check-in) or a populated keyResults list (unmeasurable, over-scoped). Regenerate expected with: bin/test-personas objectives-and-key-results-tracker --update",
